vmhal3d (JHRobotics/vmhal9x 8bc480e) vertex-array fast path. The Direct3D draw functions
(MesaVertexDrawStream/StreamIndex for DX8 streams, MesaVertexDrawBlock/BlockIndex for
DX6/7 and DrawPrimitiveUP vertices) passed every vertex to GL in immediate mode, 4-6 GL
calls per vertex. GTA 3 sends ~83-98k vertices per frame: 40 of its 60 ms per frame on the
T61 (16.5 fps standing at the first gameplay spot). When the D3D vertex layout maps 1:1 to
GL client arrays, one glDrawArrays/glDrawElements now draws the whole call: XYZ(W) floats,
float3 normals, D3DCOLOR diffuse as a GL_BGRA colour array, float1-4 texcoords per stage
(D3DTSS_TEXCOORDINDEX honoured), and D3DMCS_COLOR1 material sources through
GL_COLOR_MATERIAL when they map to one GL mode (on only around the draw: Mesa ignores
glMaterial for tracked params while it is on). Pretransformed XYZRHW, vertex blending,
flat shading, projected texcoords, specular-sourced materials and other layouts keep the
immediate path. GTA 3: 17.9 -> 24.3 fps at the same spot, picture unchanged.
C:\vmhal.slow switches the fast path off (A/B). Strip the CRs of mesa3d_draw.c and
mesa3d_api.h first (upstream is CRLF). Apply after vmhal3d-staledelete.patch.

